3623:1. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §0:25](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:25), [§5.2:263](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:263).** The guide promotes short-horizon first-action `U(a,s)` to the central reusable supervision construction without giving equal status to its measured limits: noisy labels, failed aligned-teacher Gate 4, non-additive first-action and continuation effects, and constant closed-loop policies ([journal report:38](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_JOURNAL_ROUND2_REPORT.md:38), [journal report:105](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_JOURNAL_ROUND2_REPORT.md:105)). The aligned test has wide CIs on Ackley and Hartmann, so it rules out neither all first-action value nor the observed failure on this protocol. **Fix:** make schedule/continuation-level labeling and a matched closed-loop test the next decision point before treating more first-action labels as the main route.
3625:2. **[MAJOR] [Guide §5.2:267](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:267), [§8:355](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:355).** The meta-level plan jumps toward configuration labels and transfer without a cheap answer to its own §4.4 concern that switching advantage may be nonpositive. **Fix:** first run a small paired configuration-versus-continue screen on fixed task signatures, shared warm-start data, and an explicit cost budget; build meta supervision only if a detectable advantage and signature interaction survive.
