3640:3. **[MAJOR] [Guide §1.1:47](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:47), [§2.4:159](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:159).** The architecture presents AF choice, AF parameters, and batch size as current decision actions, while the eight-action table contains one fixed surrogate acquisition action and sampling modes. **Fix:** distinguish the proposed action space from the implemented menu.
3642:4. **[MAJOR] [Guide:14](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:14), [§7:337](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:337), [§9:368](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:368).** The required sync is incomplete: Bull and GP-UCB support central body claims but are absent from §7; terms central to the rules, including `gold_probs`, `A(s)`, and Gates 4/5, are undefined in §9. Conversely, cost-aware stopping and transferred search spaces appear only in §7. The claim that §7 anchors have local PDFs is also false for several entries. **Fix:** make §7 a checked claim-to-source map and define the operative terms in §9.
3646:1. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §0:22](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:22), [§1.1:51](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:51).** The executor does **not** fit after every evaluation. Evaluation invalidates the fit; GP-dependent actions fit when needed, and RETRAIN fits without evaluating ([executor:62](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/actions/executor.py:62), [executor:99](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/actions/executor.py:99), [backend:285](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/backend/bocode_botorch.py:285)). The eight enum names themselves match [models:25](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/actions/models.py:25). **Fix:** describe the actual lazy-fit lifecycle and decide whether a new mandatory-fit behavior is intended.
3648:2. **[MAJOR] [Guide §9:392](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:392), [§3.4:222](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:222).** `U` has **six** terms, including a STOP opportunity penalty; its code default is `w_stop_opportunity=0.75` ([utility:42](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/rollout/utility.py:42), [utility:110](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/rollout/utility.py:110)). [THEORY §0:23](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:23) itself incorrectly says that default is zero. `gold_probs` is a softmax of valid rollout utilities, sometimes over a sampled action subset ([generator:423](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/generator.py:423)). **Fix:** reconcile the guide, THEORY, and defaults; specify the labeled action set.
3650:3. **[MAJOR] [Guide §4:245](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:245), [§6.2:301](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:301).** Records carry a hard-coded `utility_version="phase8.6b"` plus selected configuration metadata, but no schema or harness version stamp and no increment/check mechanism ([generator:548](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/generator.py:548), [decision_record:51](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/decision_record.py:51)). **Fix:** mark version freezing as a proposed contract and specify the stamp, compatibility check, and migration rule.
3652:4. **[MAJOR] [Guide §5.4:281](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:281).** “RLCD significantly exceeds RF” needs an arm and seed stream. On the original held-out stream, the **BT baseline** exceeds RF, while RLCD proper versus RF has a CI crossing zero ([CI artifact](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/exp_rlcd_ci.json)); on the independent 100–119 replication, both contrasts are positive ([replication artifact](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/exp_rlcd_loo_confirmatory_replication_s100_119.json)). Fine-tuned policies then collapse to constants in closed loop ([progress:139](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:139), [progress:217](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:217)). **Fix:** name the objective, arm, stream, metric, and closed-loop result.
3654:5. **[MAJOR] [Guide §6.5:329](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:329), [§8:359](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:359).** Rich-state A/B is presented as pending, but it has run: gold-argmax agreement was 0.133 in both conditions, at 2.1× tokens ([report:28](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_LENZ_JEV_REPORT.md:28)). **Fix:** report the completed negative result and retain its small-sample caveat.
3656:6. **[MAJOR] [Guide §5.4:285](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:285).** Gate 5 did not establish label-side `ρ=1` as an empirical must-pass property: bucket **median** Spearman was 1, but some records flipped argmax and the predeclared joint gate failed in 2/17 buckets ([affine report:59](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_AFFINE_REPORT.md:59)). Gate 4 stop-gain compares a gold-first-action continuation against stopping; it does not show that a learned STOP policy gains value ([validation:269](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/validation.py:269)). **Fix:** state each gate’s actual estimand and pass status.
3658:7. **[MINOR] [Guide §7:349](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:349).** The checked LMABO figures are correct: RP 1.21, four AUC deltas, fallback 0.11%, and Table 5’s 7.42 versus 109.18 minutes appear in the [local PDF](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/pdfs/arxiv_2602.07904.pdf). **Fix:** identify 7.42 minutes as the Gemini arm’s reported average for 50 iterations, since some benchmark budgets are longer.
3664:1. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §2.2:126](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:126), [§3.1:183](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:183).** Bull 2011 does **not** make per-round MLE a convergence requirement: it gives counterexamples where standard sequential parameter estimates fail to converge and develops alternative estimators. See the [paper’s summary](https://jmlr.org/papers/v12/bull11a.html). **Fix:** remove the claimed theorem mandate and state the precise assumptions of any bound the project actually intends to use.
3666:2. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §2.3:144](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:144), [§3.3:202](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:202).** Mid-episode model switching invalidates a *particular fixed-model theorem’s assumptions*; it does not make a theorem unstatable, attribution impossible, or data intrinsically incomparable. A logged switching rule is a definable adaptive algorithm, and controlled comparisons remain possible. Conversely, a calibrated PFN posterior does not by itself inherit a GP regret bound. **Fix:** frame C-class as a project protocol for specified estimands, with explicit exceptions and proof obligations, rather than a universal mathematical prohibition.
3668:3. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §3.4:222](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:222).** The stated P1 repair is algebraically wrong: if an unnormalized `Δsur` is α-*equivariant*, its weighted term changes by α. The term must be invariant or divided by an α-equivariant scale. [THEORY’s scope wording](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:63) needs the same correction. **Fix:** write the transformation equation for every nonzero utility term and test the resulting full label distribution.
3670:4. **[MAJOR] [Guide §3.2:190](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:190), [§9:375](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:375).** Adaptedness does not require a deterministic policy or temperature zero: randomized decisions are adapted when their randomness is included in the decision-time information. Temperature zero alone also does not guarantee reproducible execution. The glossary’s minimization regret `f(x*) − min_t f(x_t)` has the wrong sign; this repo internally maximizes ([backend:335](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/backend/bocode_botorch.py:335)). **Fix:** define the filtration and randomization, and use a nonnegative regret formula with an explicit objective convention.
3672:5. **[MAJOR] [Guide §4:236](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:236).** Warm-start observations can be reused, but “theorem applies as usual conditional on initial data” omits adaptive selection of that data, counted budget, noise/prior assumptions, and whether the theorem is uniform over admissible initial histories. The meta process is also not an ordinary stationary bandit when configurations share observations, consume a remaining budget, and depend on earlier outcomes ([§1.2:72](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:72)). **Fix:** specify a stateful meta estimand and prove or cite guarantees under its actual history and budget model.
3674:6. **[MAJOR] [Guide §3.4:225](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:225), [§4:243](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:243).** P2’s `D` is a one-step upper bound under a fixed state distribution and utility; P3’s nonpositive-advantage conclusion requires a pointwise, matched-continuation premise. Neither “no arm significantly beat RF” nor a small `D` establishes `A(s)≤0` at every state or closed-loop futility. [THEORY explicitly limits P2](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:111), while [P3 defines its premise](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:120). **Fix:** make gate 3 a stated, uncertainty-aware screening test, with closed-loop evaluation required for value claims.
3676:7. **[MAJOR] [Guide §1.1:58](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:58), [§6.4:316](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:316).** Multi-objective support cannot be obtained by swapping only AF and output plugins: the backend uses `SingleTaskGP` and scalar `best_f`, state extraction reads objective column zero, and rollout utility subtracts scalar best values ([backend:304](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/backend/bocode_botorch.py:304), [extractor:148](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/state/extractor.py:148), [rollout:242](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/rollout/rollout.py:242)). Hypervolume also needs a reference point. The [MO-JES paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.02905) supports an AF family, not this implementation claim. **Fix:** specify the required vector-valued model, state, utility, metric, and validation changes.
3680:1. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §6:292](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:292).** The rulebook leaves the supervision pipeline legally undefined: utility weights and scales, continuation policy, horizon, gold temperature, action-subset quotas, rollout replication and teacher-noise policy can all change labels without changing an action or state feature ([generator:171](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/src/opt_agent/dataset/generator.py:171)). **Fix:** give label construction its own classified, versioned procedure with reliability, invariance, and outcome-alignment checks.
3682:2. **[MAJOR] [Guide §6.1:294](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:294), [§6.2:301](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:301), [§4:245](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:245).** The procedures omit candidate-factory, prompt, data-consumer, replay, and comparison updates; “increment version” names machinery that does not exist. No repository check enforces episode-boundary changes or rejects incompatible dataset versions. **Fix:** define concrete change targets and a validation gate before declaring violations to invalidate conclusions.
3684:3. **[MAJOR] [Guide §5.4:279](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:279).** Success criteria have no paired failure or kill criteria, despite failed Gate 2/4 and constant-policy collapse. **Fix:** set prespecified stop conditions for teacher reliability, incremental closed-loop value over the best constant/schedule, cost, and meta-level advantage before expanding the pipeline.
3688:1. **[BLOCKER] [Guide §0:25](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:25), [§5.2:263](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:263).** The guide promotes short-horizon first-action `U(a,s)` to the central reusable supervision construction without giving equal status to its measured limits: noisy labels, failed aligned-teacher Gate 4, non-additive first-action and continuation effects, and constant closed-loop policies ([journal report:38](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_JOURNAL_ROUND2_REPORT.md:38), [journal report:105](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/runs/EXP_JOURNAL_ROUND2_REPORT.md:105)). The aligned test has wide CIs on Ackley and Hartmann, so it rules out neither all first-action value nor the observed failure on this protocol. **Fix:** make schedule/continuation-level labeling and a matched closed-loop test the next decision point before treating more first-action labels as the main route.
3690:2. **[MAJOR] [Guide §5.2:267](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:267), [§8:355](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:355).** The meta-level plan jumps toward configuration labels and transfer without a cheap answer to its own §4.4 concern that switching advantage may be nonpositive. **Fix:** first run a small paired configuration-versus-continue screen on fixed task signatures, shared warm-start data, and an explicit cost budget; build meta supervision only if a detectable advantage and signature interaction survive.
3692:3. **[MAJOR] [Guide §8:353](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/RESEARCH_BOUNDARY_GUIDE.md:353).** The open-problem order underweights the strongest positive result—BT ranking transfer on the independent stream—and leaves the completed rich-state negative test as future work ([progress:375](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:375), [progress:414](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:414)). **Fix:** prioritize a locked transfer evaluation and a schedule-value experiment, then revisit state enrichment or meta learning only where those screens show room to improve.
