runs/EXP_FINAL_GOAL_CLOSED_LOOP_REPORT.md:54:## RQ3: actual API cost already recorded, generalization still open
runs/EXP_FINAL_GOAL_CLOSED_LOOP_REPORT.md:56:The existing five-family BOCoDe joint experiment records **739 full-LLM calls / 537,456 tokens** versus **447 LLM calls / 324,702 tokens** for the frozen dimension router: about **39.5% fewer calls and 39.6% fewer tokens**. This is a development-panel cost audit. The same dimension rule failed to show a performance gain over Surrogate on the held-out IOH panel, and it is not a calibrated confidence/OOD router. A new real-LLM threshold sweep remains necessary for the intended RQ3 claim.
runs/EXP_FINAL_GOAL_CLOSED_LOOP_REPORT.md:70:On the original Rastrigin development seeds 0–9, a **post-hoc** fixed schedule of ten global decisions followed by local decisions averaged terminal best **−99.12**, versus **−109.76** for the recorded LLM and **−127.30** for AlwaysSurrogate. The schedule-minus-LLM paired mean is +10.64 [ +1.33, +22.11 ], but it wins only 4/10 seeds, and the schedule was derived after inspecting these same LLM trajectories. On separate seeds 100–119 the same schedule averaged **−126.51**, worse than Surrogate **−115.36** and Local **−113.78**. Thus the observed LLM action pattern does not establish a transferable causal mechanism.
runs/EXP_FINAL_GOAL_CLOSED_LOOP_REPORT.md:74:The current learned RF is a valid negative control and a useful diagnostic instrument, **not** a demonstrated better optimizer. A final-method paper should not claim general learned-policy superiority or transferable dimension routing from these runs. The next method experiment should replace short-horizon utility targets or action handling, freeze it on development data, and compare against Surrogate and Local on a truly untouched full-loop panel. Real System-1/System-2 cost-frontier work requires a configured LLM credential; engineering transfer requires a simulator or task definition.
